  "notes": "Phase 2 pilot: configured station-specific HTML feeds, event date and venue must be grounded in article. Never infer whole-month calendar or date from publication timestamp. Expanded with verified Fukui, Osaka and two Wakayama official station/onsite feeds. Multi-event Wakayama notices require section-specific date plus venue and are not whole-month events. Gap-prefecture-first expansion: six previously unconfigured prefectures (Iwate, Yamagata, Fukushima, Shizuoka, Yamaguchi, Ehime). Specialty article modes require article-local dates; no calendar month guessing. Verified additional official sources for Yamaguchi, Fukui, Osaka and Miyazaki; Kumamoto tourism listing is acceptable ONLY with explicit station venue; Osaka dated venue table is strict and cannot include unrelated listings. Municipal Ehime event-listing source for the officially documented Nov 22 Yawatahama industry festival at Michi-no-Eki Minatto, accept only explicit venue and event date. New Nagasaki Himawari official biker event October 18, 2026 is explicitly station-hosted; date must be grounded in the October 7, 2026 official notice. Kagoshima Tarumizu official event article adapter complements the legacy Kyushu collector; Kanagawa review limit raised to inspect all nine event/article candidates instead of silently skipping three.",
